  "lineage": "Internet-native whisper-and-trigger audio form that coalesced on YouTube around 2009-2010; Jennifer Allen coined the term 'autonomous sensory meridian response' in 2010 to name the tingling relaxation response the recordings aim to elicit. Performers whisper directly into binaural microphone rigs (dummy-head and 3Dio ear-shaped arrays) and foreground mouth sounds, tapping, scratching, and prop crinkles as the primary sonic content, panned for close in-ear headphone listening. Canonical early channels include GentleWhispering (Maria Viktorovna) and WhispersRed (Emma Smith), with the form professionalizing across YouTube and streaming platforms through the 2010s.",
